# Rule: Async UI feedback Router

- If opening a screen, revealing components after load, or handling any
  API / local DB / SharedPreferences `await` for UI, read and follow
  `.cursor/skills/async-ui-feedback/SKILL.md`.
- Hard requirements: fade on display; clear loading for every await;
  local/fast loads force **2s** minimum loading; API uses natural duration;
  API (and local) errors show message + **tente novamente**.
- If architecture is unclear, apply `.cursor/rules/dart-architecture.mdc`.
- Source of truth: skill.
